    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d315-a1">

                <pb facs="0434" n="354" xml:id="pg354"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Wilson to Mr. Koto, Japanese minister for foreign
                        affairs.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Memorandum.]</seg></opener>
                <p>Pending the receipt of fuller expression of the views of his Government, the
                    undersigned chargé d’affaires ad interim of the United States, has the honor to
                    hand this memorandum to his excellency His Imperial Japanese Majesty’s minister
                    for foreign affairs.</p>
                <p>The registration as superficies of title to perpetual leases is not acceptable to
                    the Government of the United States without some authoritative interpretation of
                    the Japanese Government that the title under that style is not inferior to that
                    of the perpetual lease.</p>
                <p>The Government of the United States are not now prepared to concede that
                    buildings on perpetual lease are subject to taxation not specified in the
                    original lease.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Huntington
                    Wilson.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
